 "reading": "The Transformer's code is as dense as the stack's. At 24,000 updates 40 to 57% of its units are open at a byte, more in the higher blocks, and nine tenths of what a block's units pass on comes from 38 to 51% of them. Of the stack's cells 35 to 49% fire at a byte, more in the higher levels alike. Neither code grows sparser from 6,000 to 24,000 updates. A sparser code is therefore not what the Transformer has and the stack lacks. What differs is the unit: the Transformer's multiplies a gate by a value, which docs/STREAM_FORM.md prices at 0.025 against plain units.",
 "limits": "One seed of the test bed's plain pair at 3e-4. Open and firing are not the same measure: a smooth gate passes a little where its drive is below zero, which the share of units passing nine tenths accounts for. Nothing here was measured at full size."
}
